{"c":[{"id":"d41c0404cc1444a5","sum":"T1-A17: NSSpellChecker's orthography is only a start (auto language lets French pass under en); the rig VM can raise a Setup Assistant page mid-job, so jobs run RIG_BIN/rig-dismiss-setup.py in a watcher loop.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T170510Z-ca62d5f751cbf8cc","text":"NSSpellChecker requestChecking treats the orthography option as a starting point: with the system's automatic language on, French text passes under en and tres passes under fr (T1, macOS 26.6).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T174001Z-5299fa2e9eaa69bd","text":"A17: the rig VM can bring a Setup Assistant page to the front mid-job; jobs run RIG_BIN/rig-dismiss-setup.py in a watcher loop, or every later step loses TextEdit's foreground.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b72cc8dfd3b4c876","sum":"A17: host and helper goldens once clashed on host-memory-7 (since renumbered, find lines by id); in TextEdit an AX write into an empty document leaves Undo disabled while a pid-posted Cmd-V shows Undo Paste, and after real typing an AXSelectedText insert undoes cleanly.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T174001Z-618052a769e64342","text":"A17: host and helper goldens both used host-memory-7 (B22 offerOnItsOwn vs A16 wrote line); the host keeps the wrote line as host-memory-8, and the helper's copy still has two host-memory-7 replies.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T174001Z-c2cf5d037ade7fad","text":"A17 VM: in TextEdit an AXSelectedText or AXValue write into an empty document leaves Edit > Undo disabled, while a pid-posted Cmd-V shows Undo Paste; after real typing, an AXSelectedText insert comes off with the next Cmd-Z and the typing history survives.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
